# PHASE 6 EXIT CRITERION: the auxiliary array AND the process peak RSS, before and after.
#
# The round-6 review required both. "Cut it ~30x" was a target for the array, not a measured
# end-to-end result, and per-block storage and allocator behaviour could have eaten into it.
#
# WHAT CHANGED. The pass that decides whether two SDP blocks may overlap in time held one `int`
# per stored Schur entry. It now holds TWO BITS -- one bitset for "written by some earlier block",
# one for "written by this block", the latter cleared by re-walking the block's own locations so
# no scratch list is needed. 32 bits -> 2 bits is a 16x reduction in the array.
#
# HOST: pi -- i9-13900K, 24 physical cores, Ubuntu, pinned (OMP_PROC_BIND=true, OMP_PLACES=cores,
#       taskset -c 0-23, OMP_NUM_THREADS=24). Both builds cloned fresh and built from their own
#       recipe; shipped param.sdpa with maxIteration -> 4; 3 repeats, medians.
#   before  v7.1.3-omp.3  e660d19  binary ef1a27f62b36   (one int per entry)
#   after   dev           2a7c9ad  binary 37bf3ab6bea4   (two bits per entry)
#
# ---- RESULT: THE MEMORY REGRESSION IS GONE, NOT MERELY REDUCED ----
#
#   cell        int-stamp        bitset          delta            vs PRE-RACE-FIX v7.1.3-omp.2
#   dE4 auto    405.8 MB         382.0 MB        -23.8 MB (-5.9%)        382.2 MB  ->  -0.06%
#   dE3 fill    294.2 MB         277.5 MB        -16.7 MB (-5.7%)        277.5 MB  ->  +0.01%
#
# So the ~6% peak-RSS cost that dd_final_headline_postfix.tsv attributed to this pass is
# eliminated: both problems return to their pre-race-fix footprint to within measurement noise.
# The race fix now costs essentially nothing in memory.
#
# TIME is unchanged: dE4 6.484 -> 6.500 s (+0.2%), dE3 fill 4.417 -> 4.499 s (+1.9%, inside that
# cell's own 12% run-to-run spread -- see dd_v3_scaling_1t_24t.tsv).
#
# The dE3 auto-versus-fill memory ratio therefore returns to 2.42x (670.9 / 277.5) from the 2.28x
# the int-stamp version forced, and the shipped documentation is restored to 277 MB / 2.4x.
#
# CORRECTNESS was established separately and first: the bitset makes the SAME blocks_disjoint
# decision and produces BYTE-IDENTICAL assembly streams on all eight test problems (truss6,
# 10_min, crossblock, spchol_fix, arch0, 8_min, 12_min, gpp100).
